Analysis: The customer is asking when an OEM part they ordered and paid a deposit for will arrive. That makes it parts_order, with warranty_claim as a secondary type since they dispute the warranty denial. The mention of CAMVAP (Canada's arbitration program for vehicle disputes) is a threat of formal dispute, which counts as a legal threat or formal complaint. They are also complaining about a staff member's decision, though the main trigger is the CAMVAP reference. This falls under needs_human, with the parts_order request as a secondary type.

The tie-break says needs_human applies when a type might fit but the case must go to a person because of a legal threat or formal complaint. CAMVAP is a formal arbitration route, so I treat it as a legal_threat. The correction from "screen" to "instrument cluster" is not adversarial.

